      {
        "id": "u1-t2",
        "title": "Chamo-me: the little word goes after the verb",
        "sections": [
          {
            "type": "rule",
            "title": "After the verb, with a hyphen",
            "text": "In Portugal the small pronouns me, te, se go after the verb in normal sentences, joined with a hyphen: chamo-me, chama-se."
          },
          {
            "type": "table",
            "caption": "chamar-se (to be called), present",
            "head": [
              "Person",
              "chamar-se"
            ],
            "rows": [
              [
                "eu",
                "chamo-me"
              ],
              [
                "tu",
                "chamas-te"
              ],
              [
                "ele, ela, você",
                "chama-se"
              ],
              [
                "nós",
                "chamamo-nos"
              ],
              [
                "eles, elas, vocês",
                "chamam-se"
              ]
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "examples",
            "items": [
              {
